WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.080
I tried an experiment a couple of years

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.160
ago to prove that my new belief of

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:07.680
losing unwanted [music]

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:09.800
weight is super easy and I can maintain

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.560
it forever. I had already tried

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:14.040
everything else for so many years and

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:16.560
nothing worked. I was so depressed until

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:17.880
this experiment proved me right. I went

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.360
through decades of putting myself

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.480
through hell just to come to this

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:23.320
conclusion today that I am now sharing

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:25.440
with you. This is exactly what I did to

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:27.840
lose 50 lb of my highest weight and

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:29.400
still maintain it years later. Like with

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.720
everything in life, your mileage may

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:35.120
vary, but 40 lb took me 6 months and I

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.920
was really locked in, but the last 10 lb

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:39.160
just happened without me even thinking

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:41.080
about it. I eat everything I want,

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:43.000
whether it's healthy, not healthy, and

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:44.480
I'm 100% confident that if I went on a

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.640
3-month cruise tomorrow and I hit the

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.920
buffet every meal, I would still come

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:51.240
back and have my current body as the

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:53.400
default. This is the new baseline and

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:56.160
it's on autopilot. Obviously, there's

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:58.880
some setup involved, strategy. If you

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:01.040
have to white-knuckle it, then you've

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:03.240
already lost. Any plan that requires you

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.480
to go really hard on anything that you

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:07.960
don't like or has you swinging from one

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:09.720
extreme to the other is just not

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:11.720
sustainable. For example, if you hit

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:13.480
your goal and you so-called relax for a

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:16.520
week and your results are gone, that was

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:18.920
me for a decade. It became this constant

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:21.480
yo-yo cycle I couldn't break out of and

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:23.440
for me, I ended up struggling more and

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:25.720
more and more until one day I woke up

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:28.120
and I thought, "I can't do this anymore.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:30.000
I deserve to have my life back." So,

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:31.760
from there, I decided the only

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.400
discipline that I truly want to focus on

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:36.920
is the discipline of being my best and

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:38.640
truest self. That was the switch in my

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:40.920
brain. This may sound a little cheesy,

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:43.240
but truly, our modern-day lives actually

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:45.000
makes it so hard to feel comfortable

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:47.240
being ourselves. So, once you can find

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.800
that to be easy, everything else will be

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:50.400
easy, too, even the hard things. These

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.960
are specific lifestyle choices that I

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:54.120
can maintain for the rest of my life and

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:55.560
more importantly, I love making these

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:57.160
choices. They feel great for my

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:59.480
well-being and I'm not fighting for my

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:01.040
life anymore. I'm finally healthy. If

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:03.040
you're new here, my name is May, and my

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:05.520
podcast and community is called Stoic

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.920
Angels. We're all in on transformation,

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:09.080
building ourselves up through our

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:11.080
brains, our body, and our aura. So, if

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:13.600
that's what you're into, subscribe and

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:15.720
join the family. I have a PDF guide that

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:18.000
I made for you guys for free that you

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:20.200
can download in the description. Inside,

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:22.480
I outline all of the major points in my

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:24.280
video, so it's a companion guide, and I

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:26.360
have prompts in there for you as well.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:27.720
So, go and download it. I have chapters

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:29.440
in my videos as well, so you can skip

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:31.080
around if you want to. And I know people

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:32.760
will ask me in the comments about what

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:35.480
my height and weight is, so let's do

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:38.040
some housekeeping real quick. I'm 5'3,

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:40.360
160 cm, and my current weight is about

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:44.280
105 to 110 lb, which is within the

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:46.160
healthy BMI range of about 19 19.5. My

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:48.200
weight also fluctuates a lot, which is

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:50.720
normal. I'm naturally fit, and I also

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:52.520
have an athletic muscular body. And from

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:54.680
what I've learned, BMI is actually not

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:56.200
the ideal standard, and definitely not

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:58.800
one-size-fits-all.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:03:00.239
In fact, Asians actually have lower BMI

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.480
cutoffs, and I have looked into a few

00:03:00.239 --> 00:03:03.320
studies on this, and genetically

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:05.600
speaking, Asians tend to store more

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:06.880
visceral fat, which puts us at a higher

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:09.040
risk of diabetes and other

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:11.840
cardiovascular diseases, especially for

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:14.760
those of us in Western societies because

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:16.760
our gut biomes are also westernized. So,

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:19.320
if you're not Asian, keep in mind the

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:20.840
BMI standards for me may not apply to

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:22.239
you, but it's important to know these

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:24.160
things. Staying healthy [music] and in

00:03:22.239 --> 00:03:26.000
peak physical shape is extremely

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:28.120
important. As the saying goes, you can

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.160
have a thousand problems until you have

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:32.239
a health problem, then you only have one

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:34.440
problem. So, angels, let's do this in a

00:03:32.239 --> 00:03:36.360
healthy way. Now, in terms of standard

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:39.400
BMI, I should be considered overweight

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:41.200
at 23 instead of 25, meaning at my

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:42.959
highest weight, according to this BMI

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:45.360
chart for Asians, I was actually

00:03:42.959 --> 00:03:47.320
considered medically obese. I didn't

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:48.560
even know that until I researched this,

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:50.280
so it's very important for us to

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:52.280
understand ourselves and our bodies and

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:53.960
know what to screen for, especially if

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:55.520
we live in a place where worthy

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:57.560
minorities. Building a life that you

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:59.560
love, most people will start with the

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:02.040
end in mind, which is also something

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:04.080
that I encourage, but we don't tend to

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:06.160
do it correctly. Most will start by

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:08.200
thinking about the body that they want,

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:10.840
their goal weight, their ideal size, and

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:12.120
then reverse engineer a plan from there,

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:13.360
but that's also not the healthiest way

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.760
to do it because you've also not

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:16.959
considered what's healthy, what's not

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:18.920
healthy, because all roads lead to Rome.

00:04:16.959 --> 00:04:21.600
Some are better and worse than others.

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:24.280
My particular road to Rome was very

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:25.800
treacherous and unhealthy, and it didn't

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:27.160
get me anywhere until I decided to do

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:29.400
something different about it. So, the

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:31.240
actual question is, when you do get

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:33.320
there, what do your lifestyle habits

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:35.200
look like? What do you eat? How are you

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:36.880
moving your body? And who is the version

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:38.520
of you who lives like that? And this

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:39.840
needs to be a focus that you want to be

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:41.520
able to get to the point where you're no

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:43.840
longer trying to lose any more weight

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:46.000
because you're genuinely so happy in

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:47.240
your body. And a lot of these diseases

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:49.680
and illnesses that I've went through was

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:51.320
because I was never satisfied, and I

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:53.040
also didn't get anywhere, like even

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:55.320
objectively speaking. Decades of that

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:57.760
didn't work for me. I now focus on

00:04:55.320 --> 00:05:00.760
building habits that I really love, and

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:03.080
my body changed as a consequence. It is

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:04.480
only a side effect. When I thought about

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:06.560
weight loss like that, my weight no

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:08.160
longer becomes the center of my life. I

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:10.720
don't even think about how much I weigh

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:12.360
unless somebody asks me. So, instead,

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:14.160
I'm thinking about the habits I'm doing,

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:16.160
what's actually enriching my life and

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:18.200
making it even better. This body will

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:20.919
take care of itself when the life takes

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:23.080
care of me. So, get specific about the

00:05:20.919 --> 00:05:24.480
type of life that you want to live. What

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:26.680
do you do on a Tuesday? What does your

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:28.520
typical Sunday morning routine look

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:30.440
like? What kind of foods do you want to

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:32.560
cook and to eat? What do you choose when

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:34.680
you eat out? How often do you eat out?

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:35.960
What do you do for fun? Where do you go

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:38.200
to spend your time? And what is

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:40.040
happening in your life that makes you

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:41.480
excited to wake up in the morning? And

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:43.760
also the opposite, what makes you not

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:45.360
excited? Whoever you choose to be, that

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:47.240
is the ideal version of you. And if you

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:49.600
keep doing this, one day you will also

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:51.120
wake up with the ideal body that matches

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:53.320
that life that you want to live because

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:55.200
the life creates the body. You're just

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:56.960
living your life. Everything else is

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:58.640
only a consequence. So, start asking

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:00.160
yourself, "How do I build a life that I

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:01.360
don't want to leave to go on a diet

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:03.120
for?" Because if you're on the diet

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:04.600
right now, that diet stops today. You're

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:06.400
just a person now. You're living your

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:08.280
life. You're not on some plan anymore.

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:10.120
Home-cooked meals is another thing that

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:12.080
changed a lot for me and make things

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:13.800
automatic because right now I eat almost

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:15.680
all of my meals at home. Again, this is

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:17.880
not about discipline for my diet or

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:19.600
anything, but because one, I think that

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:21.640
the city I live in doesn't particularly

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:23.800
have very good value for food,

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:25.520
unfortunately, which means I get to

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:27.600
enjoy my home-cooked meals rather than

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:29.600
eating out all the time, which also

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:31.840
isn't that healthy. These days I eat out

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:33.600
as a social activity and also because I

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:36.000
get to eat good food sometimes I don't

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:38.080
really know how to make at home, but if

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:40.360
I'm super busy, I also get meal plans

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:41.960
delivered. Whenever my husband or I cook

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:44.600
at home, going to the grocery store

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:46.560
physically in person also forces me to

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:48.720
be very aware of everything that I'm

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:51.720
putting into my body. I'm seeing all the

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:53.400
produce, I see the protein options, and

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:55.240
what everything adds up to in my cart.

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:57.600
So, there's no hiding from what I'm

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:59.840
putting in my body or making excuses

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:01.760
because I'm watching myself make every

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:03.440
single decision. This is not the same

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:06.080
when you go to a restaurant. But when I

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:07.760
do eat out, I give myself more options

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:09.120
and I pick what sounds good for me at

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:10.440
the moment and I allow myself that

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:12.120
freedom because we have to live our

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:13.960
lives, too. But sometimes the things

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:15.720
that sound good in the moment is also

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:17.800
not the thing that makes me feel good in

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:20.280
my body tomorrow. I might get bloated or

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:22.840
something because I ate a giant grilled

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:25.640
cheese sandwich and a pie, for example,

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:27.800
but home cooking slows me down so much

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:29.600
more and it's also more likely for me to

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:31.520
have healthy meals when we do cook at

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:33.680
home. And it makes me feel more present

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:35.280
with my own food. That level of presence

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:37.120
and self-awareness is when we make

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:39.800
really good choices for ourselves, the

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:41.440
best choices. This is also why I love

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:42.880
physically going to the grocery store.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:45.480
You see me there every couple of days or

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:47.440
so. It is not a chore for me, but a nice

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:49.200
break for me. It's a nice walk, a way to

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:50.360
get my steps in. Even if I just need to

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:51.960
take a walk, I'll just walk to the

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:54.120
grocery store and get whatever I want

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:55.600
because I'm also actively planning the

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:57.000
choices that I'm going to be making for

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:58.520
the week. So, I already feel good about

00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:00.160
doing that. If I'm not sure how any

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:02.240
particular food might fit into my

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:03.880
macros, we don't have to guess anymore.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:05.800
There's so much technology built around

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:07.800
this and eventually you will know in

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:09.480
your head. But, if you're new to this,

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:11.200
having the numbers in front of you at

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:12.919
least in the beginning as you ease into

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:14.919
this new lifestyle that you love is

00:08:12.919 --> 00:08:16.480
exactly how you will eventually get

00:08:14.919 --> 00:08:18.000
there. I like to use apps to track my

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:19.520
progress. So, this one that I'm using is

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:21.000
called Lose It. They make it easy to

