you to think about tracking in that way.

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:02.160
You're tracking until your awareness of

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:03.839
what you're eating becomes more or less

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:05.960
automatic. You don't have to do this

00:09:03.839 --> 00:09:07.360
forever, but if you want to, you can.

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:08.839
The whole point of doing this exercise

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:11.040
is just to be able to stay accountable

00:09:08.839 --> 00:09:14.040
to yourself and learn more about your

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:15.720
own eating habits. I also do 80/20 as my

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:17.160
maintenance and I don't even think of it

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:19.480
that formally. It's just how I live my

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:21.400
life. This means 80% of the time I'm

00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:22.680
eating what I just described. Mostly

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:24.120
home-cooked meals. I make sure I'm

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:26.400
getting some form of protein, some

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:28.720
gut-friendly ingredients, vegetables, a

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:30.040
carb, some fat. Most of this stuff comes

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:31.880
from my grocery cart so I know what I'm

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:33.920
getting. And if you see my fridge, baby,

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:35.680
it's mostly condiments, pickle jars,

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:38.160
fermented foods, and fruits, veggies,

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:40.000
protein. I truly love eating this way

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:41.440
and every bite is like self-care to me

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:44.320
because I know it's nutritionally

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:46.400
valuable, but the remaining 20% I truly

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:48.160
eat whatever I want. I love having

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:50.280
dessert. If I have munchies, I'll get a

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:52.000
bag of chips, no big deal, a croissant

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:53.520
on Sunday morning with my coffee, I'll

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:54.840
have my birthday cake on my birthday,

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:57.360
try out new restaurants, and if I'm

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:59.520
traveling, I am definitely eating new

00:09:57.360 --> 00:10:01.440
cuisines, snacking on things I've never

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:03.120
had before because that 80% is so

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:06.560
integrated into my life and I enjoy it

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:08.480
so much. The 20% will not undo anything

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:10.840
for me. I can always come back from a

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:12.560
weekend of eating out and I am still the

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:14.200
same weight. Even if it does change,

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:15.720
I'll just go back to my regular schedule

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:17.440
and any kind of bloating weight will be

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:18.960
gone in a couple days. This is what a

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:20.680
good maintenance plan actually feels

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:22.480
like. Nothing is forbidden, there are no

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:24.120
forbidden foods unless it makes you sick

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:26.480
or you're allergic to it, of course, but

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:28.640
essentially there is no cheat day

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:30.600
because there is nothing to cheat on.

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:32.920
This is just how I eat and because I

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:35.640
don't deprive myself, I also don't

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:37.520
binge. Your deprivation is exactly what

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:39.480
causes the binge and not the cookie, for

00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:42.160
example. I had to learn this the hard

00:10:39.480 --> 00:10:44.680
way because I totally see being deprived

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:46.560
of something as part of a larger

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:48.480
scarcity mindset, especially with

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:50.080
something that you actually want. I had

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:52.280
to spend some time unlearning these

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:55.160
habits because it never served me and I

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:56.920
always lose to it. This is a form of

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:58.480
addiction, too, you guys, just like

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:00.520
anything else that we can get addicted

00:10:58.480 --> 00:11:02.440
to. So, for example, that pie that I'm

00:11:00.520 --> 00:11:04.240
not letting myself eat will constantly

00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:06.720
be ruling over me and haunt me and I'll

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:08.600
always have cravings until I eat it.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:11.240
But, if I let myself have whatever and I

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:13.000
tell myself that every time, I literally

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:15.600
don't even think about that pie at all.

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:17.640
Life is such a paradox and we have to

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:19.880
play the game accordingly. So, if you

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:21.040
can just let yourself be free of that

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:22.560
mindset where you're not letting

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:24.160
yourself do this or do that or eat

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:26.880
anything or do certain things, your body

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:29.880
will also feel freer and be able to let

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:32.000
go of the weight easier, I promise you.

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:34.040
Staying active and curious, just like

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:36.840
how people tend to think about what they

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:39.480
do and don't identify with, I stopped

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:41.920
identifying myself as someone trying to

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:44.120
lose weight. Instead, I identify as

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:47.000
someone who is constantly active and who

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:49.200
is actively curious. And that identity

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:51.200
comes before every other choice that I

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:52.920
make because those choices are like a

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:55.360
result of the identity that I decided

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:57.760
for myself. So, whenever I come across a

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:59.680
new fitness class, a new sport, or maybe

00:11:57.760 --> 00:12:02.120
a new gym opens around me, I will be

00:11:59.680 --> 00:12:03.520
curious about it. And it is not because

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:05.320
I need to find more reasons to burn

00:12:03.520 --> 00:12:07.040
calories, but because I just enjoy

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:09.040
learning about new things, trying new

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:10.640
things. I love to move and to be in my

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:13.280
body doing things I've never done

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:16.280
before. And this curiosity keeps me

00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:18.960
trying new things. And being active is

00:12:16.280 --> 00:12:20.920
only the form that curiosity takes in my

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:22.600
body. So, decide who you are before you

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:24.080
decide on what you do because all the

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:26.560
choices that you make will get so much

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:29.560
easier once you can let your identity or

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:31.920
yourself concept do all of the work for

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:33.560
you. There's also movement as a hobby.

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:35.400
And I want to be very specific when it

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:36.880
comes to fitness because typical fitness

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:39.000
advice that you see online is a lot of

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:41.280
lifting heavy, eating a lot of protein,

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:43.640
tracking your macros. And that works for

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:46.000
many, many people. It worked for me for

00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:47.240
a while, but long-term, I ended up

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:49.240
learning that I didn't like to lift

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:50.560
heavy all the time. And I will get into

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:52.600
it in a bit throughout this video, but

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:54.360
instead, I just made it my goal to be

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:56.280
active because I love being active. So,

00:12:54.360 --> 00:12:58.200
I'm back to doing yoga several times a

00:12:56.280 --> 00:12:59.640
week, different styles, trying out new

00:12:58.200 --> 00:13:01.600
studios, different instructors.

00:12:59.640 --> 00:13:03.160
Eventually, I might just find my new

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:04.760
home. So, I'm getting back into

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:06.440
something like aerial yoga, for example,

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:07.839
which is so insane and humbling for me

00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:09.640
and fun at the same time because

00:13:07.839 --> 00:13:11.680
whenever I get back into it, literally,

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:13.400
I get the spins, which is not the fun

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:15.000
part, but I also feel really floaty and

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:16.280
graceful, which makes me feel beautiful.

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:17.720
The beginning is always the hardest

00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:19.760
part, okay? It's always a struggle, but

00:13:17.720 --> 00:13:21.160
eventually, I will get to a point where

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:23.080
I won't get so much of the spins

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:24.960
anymore. I'm also getting back into

00:13:23.080 --> 00:13:26.800
other things like pole fitness,

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:28.760
choreography, working on becoming more

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:31.480
graceful with my body, building up more

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:32.880
muscle memory as an actual skill. I'm

00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:34.520
also getting a kayak and paddle board

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:36.440
membership because I live in a city with

00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:38.120
amazing access to the water, and I'm

00:13:36.440 --> 00:13:39.800
already in love with being out there for

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:41.600
hours. Even back when I used to own a

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:43.240
boat, I would have my paddle board that

00:13:41.600 --> 00:13:44.520
I would take out for hours. I didn't

00:13:43.240 --> 00:13:46.960
even think of paddle boarding as a

00:13:44.520 --> 00:13:48.840
workout, but technically, I am in the

00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:51.080
water working every muscle in my body,

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:53.000
my arms, my core, my legs for hours at a

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:54.280
time, and I always come back sore. So,

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:56.160
the difference between fitness as a

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:58.720
workout versus as a hobby is that your

00:13:56.160 --> 00:14:00.240
motivation can change. I think you only

00:13:58.720 --> 00:14:01.640
need to rely on motivation when you're

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:03.160
doing something that you don't really

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:05.040
want to do, but when you're naturally

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:06.760
motivated to do something because you

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:08.280
love it, motivation means nothing.

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:09.480
You're naturally drawn to the activities

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:11.640
that you're choosing because it's just

00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:13.320
simply a part of your typical week, and

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:15.680
you love it, and you look forward to it.

00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:17.880
This is the same for our self-image. I

00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:20.040
look good because I enjoy being in my

00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:22.040
body, and I radiate that inside out, and

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:23.920
not the other way around, which is also

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:25.440
related to my point on stress and

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:27.080
nervous system, and this is one of the

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:28.920
most important points that I will ever

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:30.680
say in this video. Nobody's really

00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:33.080
talking about it enough, especially when

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:35.160
it comes to weight loss. This is all

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:37.920
science-backed. If you don't manage your

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:39.839
stress correctly, that stress will make

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:41.920
you hold on to your weight and make it

00:14:39.839 --> 00:14:44.360
difficult for you as a whole. This is a

00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:46.320
biological fact. When I was chronically

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:48.760
stressed, I could not lose weight to

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:50.560
save my life. I was constantly

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:52.600
fluctuating and plateauing, and I could

00:14:50.560 --> 00:14:55.200
see my scale after months and months of

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:57.240
dieting, it wouldn't move, and I

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:59.120
defeated because when your nervous

00:14:57.240 --> 00:15:01.200
system does not feel safe, your body

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:03.160
will not let the weight go. And why does

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:04.920
your nervous system not feel safe? Maybe

00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:06.560
it's because at the time I was

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:08.080
constantly telling my body that I don't

00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:10.600
deserve to eat this, I don't deserve

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:12.720
that. I was beating myself up, and I

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:14.240
didn't even know it. So, in a way, your

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:16.280
body's not keeping the weight to punish

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:18.440
you, but to actually protect you because

00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:20.960
your body sees your lifestyle as a

00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:22.800
threat. It feels unsafe, especially the

00:15:20.960 --> 00:15:24.480
way that you're talking about yourself,

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:25.920
about your food that you're eating.

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:27.720
You're constantly focusing on what you

00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:30.400
don't have instead of what you do have.

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:31.880
So, naturally, your body hangs on to

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:33.600
your weight for dear life like

00:15:31.880 --> 00:15:35.680
insurance. And when your body doesn't

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:37.120
trust that the situation is good, it

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:38.960
would do everything to hold on to the

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:40.600
weight. Some people may argue things

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:42.520
like, "Well, I don't eat so much and

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:44.760
after a while I do lose weight." Sure,

00:15:42.520 --> 00:15:46.600
but are you healthy? And is this

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:48.440
sustainable for you? Guys, I'm so

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:51.040
serious when I'm saying unhealthy eating

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:53.360
is a major glow down on every other

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:54.960
aspect of your physical appearance. And

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:57.280
I'm not even just talking about how much

00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:59.600
you weigh because society focuses on

00:15:57.280 --> 00:16:01.440
that so much when truly the more

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:03.680
important thing is, you know, your your

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:05.480
health signifiers. And if nothing feels

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:07.680
safe in our lives and nobody's a safe

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:09.360
person for us, we have to be that safe

00:16:07.680 --> 00:16:12.040
person. So, the actual work that we have

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:14.600
to shift our focus on is to help our

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:15.880
body feel more safe. So, little things

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:17.720
that can regulate a nervous system

00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:19.000
better like going on regular walks,

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:20.800
getting sunlight when you wake up in the

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:23.160
morning. And as for me, obviously, after

00:16:20.800 --> 00:16:25.240
my SPF, also drinking water, breathing

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:27.600
more slowly, being more relaxed in the

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:29.360
body in general. And like we don't have

00:16:27.600 --> 00:16:31.000
to rush anywhere. I know sometimes when

00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:32.440
I talk I get so excited and I'm just a

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:34.560
little bit spazzy, but that's just the

00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:36.320
way I am and that's okay, too. That's my

00:16:34.560 --> 00:16:39.080
identity. But because this is exactly

00:16:36.320 --> 00:16:41.600
the way I am, it especially helps people

00:16:39.080 --> 00:16:43.960
like me to spend more time in nature and

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:46.360
be more comfortable with even things

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:47.800
like touching your body, caring for

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:49.640
yourself, you know, hugging yourself,

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:51.760
surrounding yourself with people who

00:16:49.640 --> 00:16:54.200
feel safe for you, and just living your

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:55.960
life more. Log off more often so that

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:58.520
you're not constantly being bombarded

00:16:55.960 --> 00:17:01.280
with irrelevant opinions and be creative

00:16:58.520 --> 00:17:02.880
and focus on being creative. I swear to

00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:05.199
you, all of these things will help you

00:17:02.880 --> 00:17:06.920
feel and process your emotions more, and

00:17:05.199 --> 00:17:09.160
you're going to be braver about facing

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:11.079
your difficult feelings instead of

00:17:09.160 --> 00:17:12.920
eating your feelings like it's the easy

00:17:11.079 --> 00:17:15.040
way out. And we have learned, for some

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:17.160
of us, that it is absolutely not the

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:19.720
easy way out. It is just a negative

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:21.880
consequence and it shows up on our body.

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:23.880
When my nervous system is regulated,

00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:26.319
food is simply there for me to eat when

00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:28.120
I'm hungry. That's it. It's not comfort.

00:17:26.319 --> 00:17:30.600
Sometimes it's enjoyment, but it's not

00:17:28.120 --> 00:17:33.640
used as a form of punishment or reward.

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:35.120
And it's also not tied to who I am at

00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:36.960
all. It's just something that exists and

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:38.600
I also need it as fuel for my body, but

00:17:36.960 --> 00:17:40.440
to me that is the healthy way of looking

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:42.080
at food and healthy stress management

00:17:40.440 --> 00:17:43.760
and nervous system regulation will

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:46.000
definitely help. There are other things

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:48.120
that I use to regulate system as well

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:49.800
including hypnosis. There's a lot of

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:51.960
weight loss hypnosis out there that

00:17:49.800 --> 00:17:53.240
helps me regulate my eating patterns

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:54.840
better [music] subconsciously,

00:17:53.240 --> 00:17:56.640
affirmations, subliminals, things like

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:59.280
that. As part of my membership program

00:17:56.640 --> 00:18:01.000
Stoic Angels 2.0, I am creating an

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:03.120
in-depth modular system that is

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:04.760
specifically focused on weight loss,

00:18:03.120 --> 00:18:06.800
nervous system regulation, and

00:18:04.760 --> 00:18:08.160
magnetism. And all of these things will

00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:09.880
naturally help you glow up as a

00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:11.120
consequence. I'm still in the middle of

00:18:09.880 --> 00:18:12.560
building this at the moment, but if you

00:18:11.120 --> 00:18:14.240
want to learn more about it, sign up for

00:18:12.560 --> 00:18:15.880
my newsletter, get on my wait list so

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:17.480
that when it's finally out, you'll be

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:18.840
the first to hear about it. Especially

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:20.520
if you're already an angel member, you

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:22.280
will get additional perks, of course. I

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:23.840
love my angels. It's also very important

00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:25.080
for us to protect our sleep and you can

00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:26.960
do every other thing in this list

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:28.400
perfectly and your body will so not be

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:30.360
able to budge because if you're

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:31.920
chronically sleep deprived, like this is

00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:34.800
just not going to happen. This is simply

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:36.680
biology and specifically endocrinology.

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:38.200
Now, I'm not an endocrinologist, but I

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:40.080
know how to do research. When you sleep

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:42.120
less than 7 hours, your hunger hormones

00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:43.760
rise, your fullness hormone drops, your

00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:45.720
insulin sensitivity tanks, and your

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:47.880
cortisol stays elevated all day long.

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:49.520
Translation, you'll be hungrier, less

00:18:47.880 --> 00:18:51.280
satisfied when you do eat, and you're

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:52.960
going to be craving more sugar, and your

00:18:51.280 --> 00:18:55.120
body will be storing more fat around

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:57.240
your middle part. Again, biology. And no

00:18:55.120 --> 00:18:59.280
amount of healthy eating outworks 4

00:18:57.240 --> 00:19:01.720
hours of sleep. I sleep between 7 and

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:04.400
1/2 to 9 hours every night, no phone in

00:19:01.720 --> 00:19:06.480
bed, cool dark rooms, consistent bedtime

00:19:04.400 --> 00:19:07.720
including my weekends. I lost my fat

00:19:06.480 --> 00:19:09.280
during the season that I started

00:19:07.720 --> 00:19:11.080
sleeping better more than any other

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:13.600
season where I was trying to diet. So,

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:16.560
if you're serious about any of this,

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:18.600
sleep first, everything else second. I

00:19:16.560 --> 00:19:20.520
also had to learn detachment from my

00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:21.680
weight, and I weigh myself every day

00:19:20.520 --> 00:19:23.440
when I was tracking my weight, but I

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:25.640
only let myself do that when it becomes

00:19:23.440 --> 00:19:27.600
a pure data point for me, and not

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:29.960
something that I'm emotionally attached

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:32.560
to. And if it goes up, my day is ruined.

00:19:29.960 --> 00:19:34.600
Attachment to anything at all will make

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:36.240
you suffer more, so don't forget that.

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:37.840
So, if this daily weighing practice

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:40.120
doesn't serve you, then don't do it

00:19:37.840 --> 00:19:42.120
because so many factors other than what

00:19:40.120 --> 00:19:44.720
we eat can change the number on the

00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:46.640
scale. Sometimes we can't always see the

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:48.160
facts through our emotions. Unless you

00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:49.880
have a smart scale like mine, where I

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:51.520
track other things like hydration and

00:19:49.880 --> 00:19:52.880
muscle mass, body fat, and all of that,

00:19:51.520 --> 00:19:54.800
the number that you get on the scale

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:57.080
itself really does not accurately

00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:58.760
measure fat loss. Instead, when you do

00:19:57.080 --> 00:20:01.240
get a number on the scale, it is a

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:02.920
measure of the gravity of your body. It

00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:05.760
does not know the difference between

00:20:02.920 --> 00:20:07.360
water, food, hormone cycles, digestion,

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:09.480
if you're currently sick or not, and

00:20:07.360 --> 00:20:10.960
whatever else is going on in your actual

00:20:09.480 --> 00:20:12.920
body, and there's always a lot

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:14.680
happening. I weigh myself about once a

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:16.120
week these days in the morning. The rest

00:20:14.680 --> 00:20:17.680
of the time I track other things that

00:20:16.120 --> 00:20:20.120
actually reflect whatever's happening in

00:20:17.680 --> 00:20:22.080
my body. How my clothes fit, how I feel,

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:24.280
do my muscles ache, is my stomach

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:26.840
hurting, where is my energy at at 3:00

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:28.280
p.m., how am I sleeping, how I am when I

00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:30.160
work out. Sometimes if I do see a

00:20:28.280 --> 00:20:32.000
mirror, I will also take progress pics,

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:33.440
why not? As I've said in the beginning,

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:35.120
my weight fluctuates at least a few

00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:37.200
pounds, which is normal, and the number

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:39.360
on the scale is only one data point, and

00:20:37.200 --> 00:20:40.760
it is not the verdict on your body or

00:20:39.360 --> 00:20:43.040
how you live your life because we have

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:44.240
so much more in life going on than just

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:45.640
that. I want to tell you about the

00:20:44.240 --> 00:20:47.240
moment that I knew this was going to

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:48.680
work out for me permanently, and maybe

00:20:47.240 --> 00:20:49.880
that's how you will know, too. So, tell

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:51.480
me in the comments if you experience

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:53.000
anything similar to this. I came home

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:55.080
from a trip once where I had eaten

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:56.640
whatever I wanted. I even drank wine,

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:58.880
and I don't usually drink a lot. I don't

00:20:56.640 --> 00:21:00.440
track anything. I had pastries and pies

00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:03.120
almost every morning because I was in a

00:21:00.440 --> 00:21:05.040
city with really amazing pastries, and I

00:21:03.120 --> 00:21:07.200
would have been a fool not to have some.

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:09.600
And a few days later, out of curiosity,

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:11.400
I stepped on my scale and it was exactly

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:12.480
still the same as it was when I left.

00:21:11.400 --> 00:21:14.160
And I just stood there and I thought,

00:21:12.480 --> 00:21:16.160
"Oh, okay. This is what maintenance

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:18.960
feels like." It was the first time in my

00:21:16.160 --> 00:21:21.800
entire adult and teenage life that a

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:24.480
week of enjoying myself didn't cost me.

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:26.240
That first time my body didn't punish me

00:21:24.480 --> 00:21:29.240
back for just living my life because my

00:21:26.240 --> 00:21:32.120
body trusted that it was being taken

00:21:29.240 --> 00:21:34.160
care of. That trust is the whole game.

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:35.640
We are not trying to conquer our body,

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:37.600
but we're trying to become someone that

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:40.840
our body feels safe [music] with. When

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:42.800
it feels safe, it can easily let go of

00:21:40.840 --> 00:21:44.480
everything it was holding onto because

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:46.640
it's not in survival mode. None of this

00:21:44.480 --> 00:21:48.640
is a cookie-cutter plan, but really it

00:21:46.640 --> 00:21:50.040
follows your life, the person who you

00:21:48.640 --> 00:21:52.040
already are underneath all the

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:54.240
strategies that you've built to survive.

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:56.800
And the key is you are not chasing these

00:21:54.240 --> 00:21:58.720
plans and strategies, but also living

00:21:56.800 --> 00:22:00.600
with who you decide to be until your

00:21:58.720 --> 00:22:02.880
body realizes that you're already there.

00:22:00.600 --> 00:22:05.360
Remember, this is a lifestyle choice,

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:07.960
meaning you're living this life as long

00:22:05.360 --> 00:22:10.240
as you want to maintain your ideal. So,

00:22:07.960 --> 00:22:11.520
I believe in you, angels. I love you.

00:22:10.240 --> 00:22:13.480
Subscribe if you haven't already.

00:22:11.520 --> 00:22:15.520
Download that PDF if you haven't

00:22:13.480 --> 00:22:19.080
already. It is free for you. And yeah, I

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:19.080
will see you in the next video.

